## 1 · THE REPOS — which is which

⬜ **Fill this in with the repos on THIS machine.** One row each: where it lives, what it is, and
which rule governs it. ⭐ A repo with no governing rule is a repo someone will touch by mistake.

| Path | What it is | Rule that governs it |
|---|---|---|
| `~/<your-repo>/` | ⭐ **THE repo** — where the `.git` lives | `CLAUDE.md` (the router) |
| `~/<your-repo>/Mente/` | 🧠 the engine + this instance | `PROJECT-RULES.md` |

## 2 · WHAT IS OFF-LIMITS

⬜ The trees the AI may **not** read without permission. They must match `gates:` in
`mente.config.yml` — ⭐ if they diverge, this document is the claim and the gate is the fact.

## 3 · WHERE THE CREDENTIALS LIVE

⬜ The FOLDER, never the value. Defaults to `secrets/`, which is gitignored.

## 4 · WHICH COMMAND ANSWERS WHICH QUESTION

| You need… | Command |
|---|---|
| is the system healthy? | `bin/check-health` |
| do the blocks meet their contract? | `bin/check-blocks` |
| ⭐ the full verification | `bin/test-f0-f6` — *the only thing that matters is `failed: 0`* |

